---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleBody from '../components/sections/ArticleBody.astro';

const title = 'Are Microdose Edibles Legal in Thailand? | Baked Brand';
const description =
  'Are microdose THC edibles legal in Thailand? Yes, with Thai FDA approval. Full guide to the law, microdosing science, what 1.6mg THC feels like, and where to buy.';

const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Are Microdose Edibles Legal in Thailand?',
  description,
  image: 'https://bakedthailand.com/images/logo-color.png',
  datePublished: '2026-01-01',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Baked Brand Edibles in Thailand' },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Baked Brand Edibles in Thailand',
    logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://bakedthailand.com/images/logo-color.png' },
  },
};

const sections = [
  {
    h2: 'Yes, microdose edibles are legal in Thailand',
    html: `<p>Microdose THC edibles are legal in Thailand, provided they hold Thai FDA approval and meet the country's THC content limits for food products. Under current Thai food regulations, cannabis-infused food items must contain no more than 0.2% THC by weight, and must be manufactured in a licensed facility that has received approval from the Thai Food and Drug Administration.</p>
<p>Baked Brand's Chocolate Chip Cookie and Cannabis Caramels are the only Thai FDA-approved microdose THC edibles in Thailand. Each piece contains up to 1.6mg THC, manufactured in our own licensed factory from full-spectrum cannabis leaf sourced from Maejo University.</p>`,
  },
  {
    h2: 'What microdosing THC means',
    html: `<p>Microdosing refers to consuming sub-threshold doses of a psychoactive substance, that is, doses below the level that produces noticeable intoxication. In the context of THC, a typical microdose is considered to be between 1mg and 2.5mg. At this level, the effects are subtle: mild relaxation, a gentle mood shift, possibly a soft reduction in tension or anxiety. The kind of effect that allows you to remain fully functional, present, and in control.</p>
<p>This contrasts with a "recreational" dose in markets like the US or Canada, where a standard serving is typically 5mg to 10mg. For someone new to THC, 10mg can produce overwhelming effects: anxiety, disorientation, and an experience that puts many people off cannabis entirely. At up to 1.6mg, the experience is calibrated for new users and for anyone who wants the benefits of cannabis without impairment.</p>`,
  },
  {
    h2: 'The science of microdosing THC',
    html: `<p>The therapeutic potential of low-dose THC has been the subject of increasing research attention. A 2012 study published in the Journal of Pain found that very low doses of THC (1mg to 2.5mg) produced meaningful pain relief with minimal psychoactive side effects. A 2017 study in Neuropsychopharmacology found that low doses of THC reduced stress and anxiety, while higher doses had the opposite effect.</p>
<p>This "biphasic" effect of THC, where low doses and high doses produce opposite outcomes, is central to the rationale for microdosing. The goal isn't to get high. It's to stay at the bottom of the dose-response curve, where the beneficial effects are present without the anxiety, impairment, or disorientation that can accompany higher doses.</p>
<p>At up to 1.6mg per piece, Baked Brand's products are specifically formulated to stay within this microdose range. The dosage is consistent across every piece, manufactured under controlled conditions and independently tested.</p>`,
  },
  {
    h2: 'How Thai FDA approval works for edibles',
    html: `<p>Getting Thai FDA approval for a THC-infused food product is not a simple process. It requires:</p>
<ul>
<li>A valid food production licence for the manufacturing facility</li>
<li>Independent laboratory testing of each product batch for THC content and food safety</li>
<li>Accurate labelling that reflects the actual cannabinoid content</li>
<li>Compliance with the 0.2% THC by weight limit for food products</li>
<li>Compliance with packaging and consumer warning requirements</li>
</ul>
<p>Baked Brand went through this approval process for both the Chocolate Chip Cookie and the Cannabis Caramels line. Our products are lab-tested, accurately labelled, and manufactured in our own FDA-approved facility. We were the first company in Thailand to achieve this for a retail THC edible product.</p>`,
  },
  {
    h2: 'Where to buy legal microdose edibles in Thailand',
    html: `<p>Baked Brand products are available for delivery across Thailand, including Bangkok, Chiang Mai, Phuket, Pattaya, Koh Samui, and other cities. Orders are placed via LINE Official. Age verification (20+) is required before order confirmation.</p>
<p>We also supply wholesale to pharmacies, cafes, restaurants, bars, dispensaries, and other businesses. If you're interested in stocking Baked Brand products, contact us via LINE to discuss wholesale terms.</p>
<p>Our products are also available through <a href="/cannabis-edibles-bangkok/">Bangkok delivery</a>, <a href="/thc-edibles-chiang-mai/">Chiang Mai delivery</a>, <a href="/cannabis-edibles-in-phuket/">Phuket delivery</a>, and other city-specific pages.</p>`,
  },
  {
    h2: 'What to expect from your first microdose',
    html: `<p>If you've never tried a THC edible before, here's a practical guide for your first experience:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Start with one piece</strong> (up to 1.6mg THC)</li>
<li><strong>Wait 90 minutes</strong> before assessing the effect. Edibles are absorbed through the digestive system, which is significantly slower than inhaling.</li>
<li><strong>The effect should be subtle</strong>: mild relaxation, a gentle mood lift, possibly a slight softening of tension. You should remain fully functional.</li>
<li><strong>If you feel nothing after 90 minutes</strong>, one more piece is a reasonable next step.</li>
<li><strong>Don't take more because "it's not working"</strong> at 30 or 45 minutes. This is the most common mistake, and it results in taking too much once the first dose finally kicks in.</li>
</ul>
<p>For a detailed guide, see our <a href="/microdosing-guide/">complete microdosing guide</a> and <a href="/thc-edibles-dosage-guide/">THC edibles dosage guide</a>.</p>`,
  },
  {
    h2: 'Frequently Asked Questions',
    html: `<h3>Are microdose THC edibles legal in Thailand?</h3>
<p>Yes, provided they hold Thai FDA approval and comply with the 0.2% THC by weight limit for food products. Baked Brand's Chocolate Chip Cookie and Cannabis Caramels are Thailand's only Thai FDA-approved microdose THC edibles.</p>

<h3>How much THC is in a Baked Brand product?</h3>
<p>Up to 1.6mg THC per piece for both the Chocolate Chip Cookie and the Cannabis Caramels (available in Mango, Vanilla, and Chocolate). This is a microdose, well within the range that produces subtle effects without impairment for most people.</p>

<h3>How long do microdose edibles take to work?</h3>
<p>Typically 30 to 90 minutes, though for some people it can take up to two hours. The onset is slower than inhaled cannabis because THC must pass through the digestive system and liver before reaching the bloodstream. Set a 90-minute timer before considering a second piece.</p>

<h3>Can I buy microdose edibles if I'm a tourist in Thailand?</h3>
<p>Yes, with age verification (20+ required). Baked Brand delivers across Thailand, including to major tourist destinations like Bangkok, Phuket, Chiang Mai, Pattaya, and Koh Samui. Orders are placed via LINE Official.</p>

<h3>What's the difference between a microdose edible and a regular cannabis edible?</h3>
<p>A microdose edible contains a sub-threshold dose of THC, typically under 2.5mg, designed to produce subtle effects without impairment. A regular cannabis edible, as sold in legal markets like the US, typically contains 5mg to 10mg per serving and produces noticeable psychoactive effects. At up to 1.6mg, Baked Brand products are firmly in the microdose range.</p>`,
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  structuredData={structuredData}
  canonicalUrl="https://bakedthailand.com/microdose-edibles-legal-in-thailand/"
>
  <ArticleBody
    eyebrow="THAI FDA APPROVED"
    h1="Are Microdose Edibles Legal in Thailand?"
    sub="Short answer: yes. Microdose THC edibles with Thai FDA approval are legal to sell and purchase in Thailand. Here's the full picture on what the law says, what microdosing actually means, and where to find the real thing."
    sections={sections}
    ctaLabel="Order on LINE"
    shopeeLabel="View All Products"
  />
</BaseLayout>
